{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"oL5DFI7C0WVdnzqRfUI3Zahnbcw=","title":"Decision: schema definition format and location","message":"Where does the configurable schema live?\n(a) A file in the worktree, e.g. `.gitwork/schema.yaml`: human-edited rarely, reviewed via PR, read from HEAD/worktree with a built-in default fallback. Downside: tracker data in refs is independent of any branch.\n(b) A CRDT entity under `refs/work/config`: syncs with the tracker itself, no branch coupling, but config edits become ops and merge semantics for config are awkward.\nLeaning (a). Decide before the schema engine lands.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"lTmgj0tiqVuvgnfjEnlt6x6Z3W0=","key":"type","value":"decision"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"YBMOrjO5P2nY4/b6UXq4AOw0x90=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}